# Battle Nations Wiki API

A FastAPI service that pulls unit and building data from the
[Battle Nations Wiki](https://battlenations.miraheze.org) via the MediaWiki API,
parses infobox templates, and caches results in Redis.

## Architecture

```
Client request
      │
      ▼
┌─────────────┐
│  FastAPI    │  /units/{title}  /buildings/{title}  /search?q=
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│  wiki_service   │  orchestrates cache → fetch → parse → store
└──┬──────────┬───┘
   │          │
   ▼          ▼
┌──────┐  ┌──────────────────┐
│Redis │  │  wiki_client     │  httpx async → Miraheze MediaWiki API
│Cache │  │  (wikitext)      │
└──────┘  └────────┬─────────┘
                   │
                   ▼
           ┌───────────────┐
           │  parser.py    │  mwparserfromhell → normalised models
           └───────────────┘
```

## Quick Start

### With Docker Compose (recommended)

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up
```

### Manually

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env
# Start Redis separately, then:
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

Docs available at http://localhost:8000/docs

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| GET | `/units/{page_title}` | Per-rank stats for a unit |
| GET | `/buildings/{page_title}` | Production/cost stats for a building |
| GET | `/search?q=query` | Full-text wiki search |
| GET | `/health` | Health check |

## Example responses

### `GET /units/Trooper`

```json
{
  "name": "Trooper",
  "page_title": "Trooper",
  "unit_type": "Soldier",
  "description": "The backbone of the 95th Rifle Company.",
  "ranks": [
    {
      "rank": 1,
      "hp": 100,
      "armor": 0,
      "offense": 50,
      "defense": 50,
      "attacks": [
        { "name": "Rifle Shot", "power": 20, "damage_type": "Ballistic" }
      ],
      "extra": {}
    },
    { "rank": 2, "hp": 115, ... },
    ...
  ],
  "cached": false
}
```

### `GET /buildings/Iron_Mine`

```json
{
  "name": "Iron Mine",
  "page_title": "Iron_Mine",
  "building_type": "Resource",
  "gold_cost": 1500,
  "xp_reward": 30,
  "production": [
    { "resource": "Iron", "amount": 15, "period_seconds": 3600 }
  ],
  "cached": false
}
```

## Configuration (`.env`)

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `WIKI_BASE_URL` | `https://battlenations.miraheze.org/w/api.php` | MediaWiki API endpoint |
| `REDIS_URL` | `redis://localhost:6379` | Redis connection string |
| `CACHE_TTL_SECONDS` | `3600` | How long to cache wiki pages (seconds) |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | Python log level |

## Parser notes

Wiki pages use MediaWiki infobox templates. The parser (`services/parser.py`) looks for:

- **Units**: parameters like `hp1`–`hp9`, `armor1`–`armor9`, `offense1`–`offense9`, `defense1`–`defense9`, and `attack{rank}name` / `attack{rank}power` / `attack{rank}type`.
- **Buildings**: `production`, `amount`, `time` (accepts `1h`, `30m`, `3600` formats), `gold`, `xp`, and per-resource keys (`iron`, `coal`, `oil`, …).

If a page uses different parameter names, add them to the alias lists in `parser.py`.

## Running tests

```bash
pip install pytest
pytest tests/ -v
```